preloader-stock.img is an unmodified known-stock Miyoo Flip preloader image.
It is preserved so Zlyme can restore that exact stock revision when the
installed preloader is the apommel-patched counterpart this file was paired
with. Zlyme does not synthesize, patch, or regenerate this image.

The known copy comes from the Miyoo Flip hardware-research tree, through
the apommel multiboot app that carried it:

  Zetarancio/Miyoo-Flip-Mainline-Linux-Reverse-Engineering
  introducing commit 8ef495f5711ce13645e9c68df63b7d7a9934cf7e
  path preloader-stock-rocknix/App/apommel-multiboot/preloader-stock.img
  wiki commit c126d3235face9ddca5bf021258a84758dca543c

SHA-256:
  dfdd7d20d6fd3beb18350dcf8fa58740b40b4baaf39467d45076f949053a2922
Historical MD5:
  1d525e6e6c89bd788b5245c90c97833b

The hardware wiki records this file as byte-identical to the first 2 MiB of
spi_20241119160817.img. It also records that more than one stock SPL build
exists, so this file is that known revision, not every Miyoo preloader.
The patched counterpart is not installed. Its fingerprint is
preloader-patched.img, SHA-256
ed10591f62ae0b8845ac9bd6cf80c896a2b172d32c7c4ef6564d305e8662c13d,
historical MD5 c2009762b1704d5ed2ebbfa4346e6ecc.

The script and checker in this package are MIT. This image is Miyoo vendor
firmware. This record identifies the bytes and where the known copy came
from. It is not a license grant.

zlyme-preloader may select this file only when no per-device
mtd5-original-<sha256>.img exists and the installed preloader matches that
patched fingerprint, and only after the structure check and the DDR check
that runs before a NAND write.
